    "styles": [],
    "summaryDescription": "The Ministry of Information had the task of disseminating ideas to the British public. Its aim was to present material that would intensify certain public values - in this case, support for the war effort throughout World War II. To this effect, the Ministry staged a series of free exhibitions in central London's busy Charing Cross railway station in order to expose Britons to pro-Allied forces propaganda. In this poster, the viewer sees a view of the Royal Navy at work.\r\n\r\nIt is interesting to note that Goebbels is said to have modelled the German Propaganda Ministry on the effectiveness of the British Ministry.",
